<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal raises 136 bln esc on BFE sale.</title>
<headline>Portugal raises 136 bln esc on BFE sale.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese government will raise 136 billion escudos from its sale of state-controlled Banco de Fomento e Exterior (BFE) to Banco Portugues de Investimento (BPI), the Lisbon bourse said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>BPI offered 2,615 escudos per share in its bid for the 65 percent of BFE on offer.</p>
<p>Portuguese Finance Minister Antonio Sousa Franco said last week that Portugal would raise far more than the initially forecast 380 billion escudos from privatisations this year.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
